      <p class="pp-section-num">01</p>
      <h2>Agreement Overview</h2>
      <p>These Terms of Service ("Terms") constitute a legally binding agreement between you and MomentCast ("MomentCast," "we," "us," or "our") governing your access to and use of the MomentCast platform, including our marketing site at <strong>momentcast.live</strong>, our streamer dashboard at <strong>app.momentcast.live</strong>, and all related services.</p>
      <p>By creating an account, purchasing credits, or using any part of the platform, you acknowledge that you have read, understood, and agree to be bound by these Terms and our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>, which explains how we handle your data and use cookies.</p>
      <p>If you do not agree to these Terms, do not use MomentCast.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- 2 -->
    <div class="pp-section mc-reveal" id="s2">
      <p class="pp-section-num">02</p>
      <h2>Definitions</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>"Streamer"</strong> means any individual or entity that creates an account on MomentCast and uses the platform to broadcast live events.</li>
        <li><strong>"Viewer"</strong> means any individual who watches a live or recorded stream via a MomentCast event page.</li>
        <li><strong>"Credit"</strong> means a pre-purchased unit that entitles a Streamer to create one event with a defined allocation of viewing hours.</li>
        <li><strong>"Viewing Hours"</strong> means the cumulative total of all viewer watch time for a given event, measured in hours. For example, 50 viewers each watching for 3 hours equals 150 viewing hours.</li>
        <li><strong>"Event"</strong> means a single live stream and its associated event page, recordings, and metadata created by a Streamer.</li>
        <li><strong>"Platform"</strong> means collectively the MomentCast website, dashboard, viewer pages, API, and all supporting infrastructure.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- 3 -->
    <div class="pp-section mc-reveal" id="s3">
      <p class="pp-section-num">03</p>
      <h2>Account Registration</h2>

      <h3>Eligibility</h3>
      <p>You must be at least 18 years old and have the legal capacity to enter into a binding agreement to create a Streamer account. MomentCast is intended for professional use by photographers, videographers, and event service providers.</p>

      <h3>Account responsibilities</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>You are responsible for maintaining the confidentiality of your account credentials, including any streaming keys provided for your events.</li>
        <li>You are responsible for all activity that occurs under your account.</li>
        <li>You agree to provide accurate and current information during registration and to update your information promptly if it changes.</li>
        <li>You must notify us immediately at <a href="mailto:support@momentcast.live">support@momentcast.live</a> if you believe your account has been compromised.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>One account per person</h3>
      <p>Each individual or business entity may maintain only one Streamer account. We reserve the right to merge or terminate duplicate accounts.</p>

      <h3>Sign-in methods</h3>
      <p>You may sign in with an email address and password or with your Google account. If you use Google sign-in, we receive your name and email address from Google. Accounts created with an email address must be verified through a confirmation link we send by email. Confirmation and password reset links work once and expire after one hour.</p>

      <h3>Emails we send</h3>
      <p><strong>Service emails.</strong> We send emails that are necessary to provide the Platform, such as account confirmation, password resets, receipts, and notices about your events or these Terms. These cannot be turned off while your account is open.</p>
      <p><strong>Tips and product updates.</strong> We send these only if you opt in, either with the optional checkbox when you sign up or through the one-time prompt in your dashboard. Opting in is never required to use MomentCast, and your choice does not affect your account or your events. Every marketing email includes an unsubscribe link, and you can unsubscribe at any time.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- 4 -->
    <div class="pp-section mc-reveal" id="s4">
      <p class="pp-section-num">04</p>
      <h2>Credits, Pricing &amp; Payment</h2>

      <h3>Credit-based model</h3>
      <p>MomentCast operates on a credit-based system. Each credit entitles you to create one event with a set allocation of viewing hours. You may add additional viewing hours to an active event by applying more credits from your balance at any time.</p>

      <h3>Purchasing credits</h3>
      <p>Credits are available for purchase through the Streamer dashboard. All payments are processed securely by <strong>Stripe</strong>. MomentCast does not store your credit card number, CVV, or other raw payment data. All prices are listed in U.S. dollars (USD).</p>

      <h3>Credit packs</h3>
      <p>Credits may be offered individually or in discounted multi-credit packs. Specific pricing, pack sizes, and any promotional discounts are displayed at the time of purchase in the dashboard and are subject to change. Any price change applies only to future purchases and does not affect credits already purchased.</p>

      <h3>Credit validity</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Credits do not expire. Unused credits remain in your account until you close or delete it (see Section 12).</li>
        <li>Credits are non-transferable between accounts.</li>
        <li>Credits have no cash value and may not be resold.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Taxes</h3>
      <p>Prices displayed may not include applicable sales tax, VAT, or other local taxes. You are responsible for any taxes associated with your purchases. Tax will be calculated and displayed, where applicable, at checkout.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- 5 -->
    <div class="pp-section mc-reveal" id="s5">
      <p class="pp-section-num">05</p>
      <h2>Refund Policy</h2>

      <div class="pp-callout">
        <p><strong>Summary:</strong> Credits applied to events are fully refundable if the event is cancelled before streaming begins. Once streaming credentials have been activated, credits applied to that event are non-refundable.</p>
      </div>

      <h3>Before streaming starts</h3>
      <p>If you cancel an event before revealing or using your streaming credentials, all credits applied to that event (including any additional viewing hours purchased) will be returned to your account balance in full. This applies regardless of how many credits were applied.</p>

      <h3>After streaming starts</h3>
      <p>Once streaming credentials have been revealed or the stream has gone live, the credits applied to that event are considered consumed and are <strong>non-refundable</strong>. This includes the initial credit used to create the event and any additional credits applied for extra viewing hours.</p>

      <h3>Unused viewing hours</h3>
      <p>Viewing hours that are allocated to an event but not consumed by viewers are not refundable and do not roll over to other events. We encourage Streamers to start with the default allocation and add viewing hours only as needed during the event.</p>

      <h3>Unused credits (not applied to events)</h3>
      <p>Credits sitting in your account balance that have not been applied to any event may be eligible for a refund at our discretion. To request a refund of unused credits, contact <a href="mailto:support@momentcast.live">support@momentcast.live</a>. Refunds of unused credits will be processed to the original payment method via Stripe. Request any refund before you delete your account, because unused credits are forfeited on deletion (see Section 12).</p>

      <h3>Disputes</h3>
      <p>If you believe a charge was made in error, contact us at <a href="mailto:support@momentcast.live">support@momentcast.live</a> within 30 days of the transaction. We will review and resolve the matter within 10 business days.</p>
    </div>

